4. Private-key security gate

The original Duck snapshot contained a marker private key. CRooot removed that material from the current tree. A private key must never ship in an SDK, AAR, APK, source archive, or release artifact. The CI workflow (`android-sdk-ci.yml`) now includes a scan step that fails if private-key material (`-----BEGIN.*PRIVATE KEY-----`) is reintroduced in `sdk/` or `app/`. Any originally exposed key must be rotated or revoked outside this repository.

